				<r3d:description language="eng">The University of Guelph Research Data Repositories provide long-term stewardship of research data created at or in cooperation with the University of Guelph. The Data Repositories are guided by the FAIR Guiding Principles for scientific data management and stewardship which aim to improve the Findability, Accessibility, Interoperability and Reuse of research data. The Data Repositories is composed of two main collections: the Agri-environmental Research Data collection which houses agricultural and environmental research data, and the Cross-disciplinary Research Data collection which houses all other disciplinary research data.</r3d:description>
